    "description": "<h1 style=\"margin-right:0cm;margin-left:0cm;font-size:24pt;font-family:'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:Arial, sans-serif;color:rgb(51,51,51);font-weight:normal;\"><i>The Commonwealth Relations Office List 1951</i> is the first edition of this publication, published by His Majesty\u2019s Stationery Office 1951.</span></h1><p></p><h1 style=\"margin-right:0cm;margin-left:0cm;font-size:24pt;font-family:'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:Arial, sans-serif;color:rgb(51,51,51);font-weight:normal;\">The Commonwealth Relations Office was formed in 1947, when the Dominions and India Offices were combined.</span></h1><p></p><h1 style=\"margin-right:0cm;margin-left:0cm;font-size:24pt;font-family:'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:Arial, sans-serif;color:rgb(51,51,51);font-weight:normal;\">The last edition of the <i>Dominions Office and Colonial Office List</i> was published in 1940. \u00a0The last editions of the <i>India Office List </i>and<i> Burma Office List</i> were published in 1947.</span></h1><p></p><h1 style=\"margin-right:0cm;margin-left:0cm;font-size:24pt;font-family:'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:Arial, sans-serif;color:rgb(51,51,51);font-weight:normal;\">Digitised by Google Books from the collection at the University of Michigan</span><span style=\"font-size:16pt;font-family:Arial, sans-serif;color:rgb(51,51,51);font-weight:normal;\">\u00a0</span></h1><p></p><span style=\"font-weight:normal;\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:Arial, sans-serif;color:rgb(51,51,51);\"><a href=\"https://books.google.com/books?id=QeouC8bONrEC\" style=\"color:#0000FF;\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://books.google.com/books?id=QeouC8bONrEC</a></span><span style=\"font-size:16pt;font-family:Arial, sans-serif;color:rgb(51,51,51);\">\u00a0\u00a0</span></span>",
